[36m(main_task pid=3800193)[0m Doc 1(Title: Fram) Fram Fram (""Forward"") is a ship that was used in expeditions of the Arctic and Antarctic regions by the Norwegian explorers Fridtjof Nansen, Otto Sverdrup, Oscar Wisting, and Roald Amundsen between 1893 and 1912. It was designed and built by the Scottish-Norwegian shipwright Colin Archer for Fridtjof Nansen's 1893 Arctic expedition in which the plan was to freeze ""Fram"" into the Arctic ice sheet and float with it over the North Pole. ""Fram"" is said to have sailed farther north (85°57'N) and farther south (78°41'S) than any other wooden ship. ""Fram"" is preserved at the Fram Museum in Oslo, Norway.
