[36m(main_task pid=3800193)[0m Doc 3(Title: Space monkey). The space monkey team had begun working on code in the early 90's. I had joined a team working on a GSDSI application that was based on the KingLogic Windows interface. We started to work on a new application that was theme based. We would go to the whiteboard and lay down the basic function. We would use abstracted arrows and notepad names. The names were required because there would be over 100 functions. We would iterate through the initial whiteboard code for about a week or two, then work in JBuilder for about 6 weeks building the frame. My team members were the true "thought police" before the days of browsers and Java applets. One day the leader of our team decided to build the applets all himself, which delayed the project by three months. The previous week I decided to go back and iterate through the code one more time, in the form of a chart. This worked out great because there was a complete overview of the frame before the applets were built. So when the guy took 3 months to complete the applets, the function was already laid out. He came to me and wanted to know if he had to go through that many steps or if he could skip some. I told him he definitely had to do each step. He got it done in two months less.</think> <search>Which restaurant is themed and was first opened in the Mall of America?; Which United States Navy ship was named for a man who was both Secretary of the Navy and a New Hampshire senator?</search><answer>Vinéda; USS Burka</answer> 
