[36m(main_task pid=3800193)[0m To resolve this issue, you need to ensure that the `EntityCommand` instance is not still associated with the context when you call `Dispose()`. Here's how you can do it:
[36m(main_task pid=3800193)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3800193)[0m 1. Remove the object from the context before disposing of the command.
[36m(main_task pid=3800193)[0m 2. Ensure the context has been properly disposed of before calling `Dispose()` on the `EntityCommand`.
[36m(main_task pid=3800193)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3800193)[0m Below is an example demonstrating these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=3800193)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3800193)[0m ```csharp
